In the Cedar Lantern project (release code CL-721), I decided against automatic deletion of imported notes because the support team needs original notes to address customer-reported mistakes. The design maintains an archive for source notes and separately stores accepted summaries, requiring each summary to retain a source identifier. Morgan oversees the archive review, scheduled for October 18. We have yet to resolve whether attachments should be archived with the summaries or kept separately. The default retention is thirty days, and a failed summarization must keep the original note accessible. Previously, the cleanup process was tied to the arrival of requests, risking deletion of unreviewed work in response to unrelated requests. We shifted cleanup to a defined completed-review boundary, which is crucial to ensure notes are cleared only post thorough review, thus protecting unreviewed work from inadvertent deletion.